00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:49,510
I can't believe she cracked your code.

252
00:14:54,470 --> 00:14:58,180
All right, okay. Laurie proposes to Jo and she says no...

253
00:14:58,350 --> 00:15:02,650
...even though she's still in love with him. And then he ends up marrying Amy.

254
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:05,610
Hey.

255
00:15:05,770 --> 00:15:08,150
Mine was by accident.

256
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:09,530
All right.

257
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:13,200
The boiler explodes and destroys the hotel and kills the dad.

258
00:15:15,330 --> 00:15:16,370
Beth dies.

259
00:15:25,250 --> 00:15:27,880
Beth...? Beth dies?

260
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:33,090
Is that true? If I keep reading, is Beth gonna die?

261
00:15:33,470 --> 00:15:36,760
No, Beth doesn't die. She doesn't die. Does she, Rachel?

262
00:15:36,930 --> 00:15:39,220
- What?     - Joey's asking if you've just ruined...

263
00:15:39,390 --> 00:15:42,770
...the first book he's ever loved that didn't star Jack Nicholson.

264
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:49,570
No. She doesn't die.

265
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:51,610
Then why would you say that?

266
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:59,540
Because I wanted to hurt you.

267
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:03,960
Oh, there they are. I dropped my keys.

268
00:16:06,710 --> 00:16:08,340
Got them.

269
00:16:13,220 --> 00:16:14,380
Hi.

270
00:16:15,050 --> 00:16:17,430
Sorry. I'm sorry.

271
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:19,720
You would not believe my day.

272
00:16:20,060 --> 00:16:23,810
I had to work two shifts. And then to top it off...

273
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:28,110
...I lost one of my fake boobs in a grill fire.

274
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:32,990
What are you smiling at?

275
00:16:33,150 --> 00:16:35,450
Sorry, I was just thinking your day could still pick up.

276
00:16:41,580 --> 00:16:43,080
Hello.

277
00:16:43,790 --> 00:16:45,790
I love this friend thing.

278
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:51,630

279
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:54,800
Listen, Robert's gonna be here any second...

280
00:16:54,970 --> 00:16:57,010
...so could one of you just tell him?

281
00:16:57,180 --> 00:16:58,680
Please, right now.

282
00:16:58,850 --> 00:17:02,850
No, every time I see him, it's like, "Is it on the loose? Is it watching me?"

283
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:05,690
We can't tell him.

284
00:17:05,850 --> 00:17:08,900
You can't go up to a guy you barely know and talk about his...

285
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:11,320
...stuff.

286
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:15,320
He's right. Even if it's to say something complimentary.

287
00:17:18,780 --> 00:17:20,660
- Hey.     - Hey.

288
00:17:20,830 --> 00:17:21,870
So you ready for the gym?

289
00:17:22,040 --> 00:17:25,080
They've got this new rock-climbing wall. We can spot each other.

290
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:29,500
Yeah, I can spot you from here.

291
00:17:32,630 --> 00:17:34,130
What?

292
00:17:35,010 --> 00:17:37,550
Okay. Listen, ahem, Robert...

293
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:41,680
- Hey, don't we have to?     - Yeah, we got... Yeah. Mm-hm.

294
00:17:48,230 --> 00:17:49,980
I think you're really, really great.

295
00:17:50,150 --> 00:17:53,480
Oh, God. Here we go again.

296
00:17:53,650 --> 00:17:58,200
Why does this keep happening to me? Is it something I'm putting out there?

297
00:18:00,410 --> 00:18:04,080
Is this my fault? Or am I just nuts?

298
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:10,880
I don't know what to say.

299
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:15,800
Hey, buddy? This is a family place. Put the mouse back in the house.

300
00:18:39,030 --> 00:18:43,530
Really? Well, it's just like everyone else's apartment.

301
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:45,540
It's got, uh, rooms and walls and ceilings.

302
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:48,250
I just wanted to see where you live. Now give me the tour.

303
00:18:48,410 --> 00:18:50,500
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

304
00:18:50,670 --> 00:18:52,880
- Uh, this is the living room.     - That's nice.

305
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:54,290
All right.

306
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:57,130
- And this is the kitchen.     - That's real pretty.

307
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:59,170
Wait a minute. Don't I get to see the bedroom?

308
00:18:59,340 --> 00:19:03,390
The bedroom. Well, it's pretty much your typical...

309
00:19:04,720 --> 00:19:07,060
...bedroom.

310
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:09,480
We're still on this side of the door. Ha, ha.

311
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:11,060
Yeah, but I didn't get to see it.

312
00:19:11,230 --> 00:19:15,770
Oh, shoot. Maybe next time. Thanks for a lovely evening.

313
00:19:33,630 --> 00:19:35,500
So, um, who is she?

314
00:19:35,670 --> 00:19:39,420
Oh, ha, ha. That was the blind date I told you about.

315
00:19:39,590 --> 00:19:42,680
She called and switched it from Tuesday.

316
00:19:43,930 --> 00:19:45,640
Did you like her?

317
00:19:45,970 --> 00:19:50,770
And I'm just asking as a friend because I am totally fine with this.

318
00:19:53,270 --> 00:19:55,100
Well, you seem fine.

319
00:19:55,810 --> 00:19:59,070
Okay, you know what? I'm not fine. I'm not.

320
00:19:59,230 --> 00:20:02,990
I mean, how could I be fine? Hearing you come in with her.

321
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:05,570
She wants to see your bedroom.

322
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:14,580
You know what?

323
00:20:16,790 --> 00:20:19,130
What if we're friends...

324
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:21,710
...who don't see other people?

325
00:20:24,180 --> 00:20:25,640
You mean like exclusive friends?

326
00:20:26,470 --> 00:20:28,050
Why not?

327
00:20:28,810 --> 00:20:32,140
I mean, this has been the most amazing week.

328
00:20:33,770 --> 00:20:35,560
Would it be so terrible?

329
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:40,480
Even if we were friends who lived together?

330
00:20:42,820 --> 00:20:47,160
Or maybe someday, friends who stood up in front of their other friends...

331
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:50,740
...and vowed to be friends forever.

332
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:59,500
You know, we're back where we were.

333
00:21:01,050 --> 00:21:06,300
Honey, I would love to do all that, but nothing's changed.

334
00:21:06,470 --> 00:21:10,220
That's not true. You don't have a mustache.

335
00:21:11,930 --> 00:21:14,730
Okay. Okay, one thing's changed.

336
00:21:15,350 --> 00:21:18,850
But we still want different things, and we know how this is gonna end.

337
00:21:20,020 --> 00:21:21,610
You know what?

338
00:21:22,030 --> 00:21:24,860
I gotta walk out of here right now.

339
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:30,200
Because getting over you is the hardest thing that I have ever had to do.

340
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:34,040
Um, I don't think I could do it again.

341
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:37,000
I know I couldn't.

342
00:21:38,710 --> 00:21:40,040
Yeah.

343
00:21:42,750 --> 00:21:44,050
So...

344
00:21:52,430 --> 00:21:55,350
How about one last game of racquetball? Hmm?

345
00:22:00,900 --> 00:22:03,400
Watch the thorns.

346
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:11,870
What?

347
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:15,240
Beth is really, really sick.

348
00:22:20,750 --> 00:22:24,800
Jo's there, but I don't think there's anything she can do.

349
00:22:28,260 --> 00:22:29,680
- Joey?     - Yeah?

350
00:22:29,930 --> 00:22:32,350
You wanna put the book in the freezer?

351
00:22:33,260 --> 00:22:35,350
- Okay.     - Okay.

